{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dormant-fibre-pterosaurs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOnly 59 of the 221 bug tickets filed 7–21 Aug 2026 carry a `caused_by` link, and the most-linked target (`hemophobic-vegetarian-mynah`, 8 links) is a misattribution — its \"children\" are unrelated CI items. The link is the only machine-readable causation in the store; without it the fortnight review had to re-derive introducing commits by `git log -S` for 196 bugs, and agent-written \"pre-existing\"/\"regression\" labels were wrong 43 times. Story `major-specified-bream` measures whether `caused_by` can be auto-derived; this story makes the link trustworthy when written by hand. Approved 2026-08-21.\n\n## Approach\n(1) Validation at link time in `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` (`link`) and the MCP/CLI surfaces: a `caused_by` target must be a ticket that has at least one trailer commit reachable from `origin/main` (resolved via the existing referencing-commit scan in `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`), else the link is refused with a message naming the rule; `--force=<reason>` keeps the escape hatch. (2) A janitor/fsck check that, for each `caused_by`, the target's earliest trailer commit is not newer than the bug's introducing construct where the bug records an `introducing_sha` (new optional field on bug tickets, written by rebar-debug Step 0/Phase 1). (3) Seed: the review's dated set (196 rows, sha + date + method + confidence) is attached to this ticket as the labelled corpus for `major-specified-bream`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/link.py` (or wherever `link` is implemented), `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json` (optional `introducing_sha`), `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `tests/unit/commands/test_caused_by_validation.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: `link <bug> <ticket-with-commit> caused_by` succeeds. Edge: target with no trailer commit is refused; `--force` with reason succeeds and records the reason; fsck flags a `caused_by` whose target commit postdates the recorded `introducing_sha`. Pinning: `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py` (the link row), `tests/unit/test_fsck*.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A `caused_by` link to a commit-less ticket is refused on CLI, library and MCP with the same message; checked by the parity oracle row.\n- [ ] `rebar fsck` reports a `caused_by` whose target commit is newer than the bug's `introducing_sha`; checked by a fixture store.\n- [ ] The dated corpus is attached to this ticket as a comment or artifact; checked by `rebar show`.\n","id":"77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Make caused_by trustworthy: validate the target has a commit, fsck-check it against the bug's introducing sha"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787354787501040001,"uuid":"c847e87d-a150-491a-88b6-64daacc79d7a"}